[{:db/id "q-11790/selection/b97b2b0360b68e89267daec04b608dd52bb3d08d805b08054e729181046b55d1" :answer/id #uuid "e54861c8-af68-5715-9891-48862e43054f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=6y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11790/selection/9ccbc54c8a7c99aa32e755ee248a776c14d3fbbeb5548827e9593addab202de3" :answer/id #uuid "a2e27484-80c6-525f-a22c-6f2a76cf2ed5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=3y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11790/selection/21a85a6c16cd09920557c85d675b32af6b265d2f20288e63723a698fa6039110" :answer/id #uuid "a3de291a-f62d-568d-8c2e-8c6843e97fc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-9y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11790/selection/ae8320f65f5dba099d2a882be054b825ecf8277bd075c99859fc91ca980889a6" :answer/id #uuid "89f42cc9-9abe-5d2b-9453-325a37a2c5fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=9y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11790/selection/445f2b78a504c109d64652efa2d19bada6a62c0567e96e3fad794421fd0f4fe3" :answer/id #uuid "44474fa0-b300-5a1d-bc71-c31fcab6ecca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-6y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11790/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7775113f-aabf-5a5f-90c4-2dd40846de46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11790/selection/ae8320f65f5dba099d2a882be054b825ecf8277bd075c99859fc91ca980889a6" :answer-field/choices ["q-11790/selection/b97b2b0360b68e89267daec04b608dd52bb3d08d805b08054e729181046b55d1" "q-11790/selection/9ccbc54c8a7c99aa32e755ee248a776c14d3fbbeb5548827e9593addab202de3" "q-11790/selection/21a85a6c16cd09920557c85d675b32af6b265d2f20288e63723a698fa6039110" "q-11790/selection/ae8320f65f5dba099d2a882be054b825ecf8277bd075c99859fc91ca980889a6" "q-11790/selection/445f2b78a504c109d64652efa2d19bada6a62c0567e96e3fad794421fd0f4fe3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11790" :question/id #uuid "ae3f1372-2de8-5192-9ccc-ef2fc1ff02d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-11790" :question/problem "Find the equation of the upward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and which passes through the point $(6,4).$" :question/worked-solution "We know that for any upward or downward-opening parabola whose vertex is $(0,0),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe're told that the given parabola passes through the point $(6,4),$ so we can substitute $x=6$ and $y=4$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {6}^{2} & =4p(4) \\\\ 36 & =16p \\\\ p & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(\\frac{9}{4})y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11790/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "281514e9-6e16-5b21-ba4e-503991d811c2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11790"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11822/selection/c7d1fd0870638eccaa10182fe0c203d1742a5313cbeb74d458efc7ba2b3e5683" :answer/id #uuid "ae3809ff-f2b5-545e-9414-4dee94505a3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}=-2(y+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11822/selection/9071c5e11559e769c717c9e7fd9e8707e5c09b60ee57b17adb3cccbd374dfb30" :answer/id #uuid "fcc946d8-6a13-5497-a02f-189e9847dad8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}=2(y+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11822/selection/475b492672c8102a06218d7ff0bf351e348dcadcc4fa1713a0de29dd394d5c01" :answer/id #uuid "05363ca3-93b9-55bc-8ab7-dda9c11c0fee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}=2(y+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11822/selection/aff26145dd117f76ad1630dfacb65e2edf96685a7804ab461c11a27919f3ed49" :answer/id #uuid "a12332dd-a5b4-5fd8-8bf5-63eeb5fc083d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}=-4(y+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11822/selection/4cdd166b490715f1515fa4a6d2c747a849dcd1444996f40bf0fc31f7c4311040" :answer/id #uuid "21f91c6b-2db5-572d-afb6-f86984d26d93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}=4(y+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11822/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fc03ab09-fe27-590c-bd85-b5f8d0992319" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11822/selection/9071c5e11559e769c717c9e7fd9e8707e5c09b60ee57b17adb3cccbd374dfb30" :answer-field/choices ["q-11822/selection/c7d1fd0870638eccaa10182fe0c203d1742a5313cbeb74d458efc7ba2b3e5683" "q-11822/selection/9071c5e11559e769c717c9e7fd9e8707e5c09b60ee57b17adb3cccbd374dfb30" "q-11822/selection/475b492672c8102a06218d7ff0bf351e348dcadcc4fa1713a0de29dd394d5c01" "q-11822/selection/aff26145dd117f76ad1630dfacb65e2edf96685a7804ab461c11a27919f3ed49" "q-11822/selection/4cdd166b490715f1515fa4a6d2c747a849dcd1444996f40bf0fc31f7c4311040"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11822" :question/id #uuid "ab5a1b70-a3f1-5738-b055-95cc8bfcec5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-11822" :question/problem "Find the equation of the upward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(-1,-4)$ and which passes through the point $(1,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "For any upward or downward-opening parabola with its vertex at $(h,k),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nHere, the vertex has coordinates $(h,k)=(-1,-4).$ Substituting these into the general standard equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-(-1))^{2} & =4p(y-(-4)) \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =4p(y+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left to find the value of $p.$ We know that the given parabola also passes through the point $(1,-2),$ so we can substitute $x=1$ and $y=-2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2} & =4p(y+4) \\\\ (1+1)^{2} & =4p(-2+4) \\\\ 4 & =8p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2} & =4p(y+4) \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{2})(y+4) \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =2(y+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11822/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29e2083d-fe76-5a35-9c3a-7e6ad19ff968"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11822"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11825/selection/3d4912fba6865d84fff42ae1218f5bc1017b36b705fe0ea683a0de996c2d48c0" :answer/id #uuid "259888fb-579b-5072-8648-5b6b3798e8c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{2}{3}(y-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11825/selection/82ae299ea8c2505291695068a185902058180804be81fb94e5f22ded483c2bcf" :answer/id #uuid "24f88ff7-2937-5f35-86c6-7eb2bf033680" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}=-\\frac{4}{3}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11825/selection/b84dbb196368112b67963012d5eb95628a68cbc3e7ebc3754fae1a2791231677" :answer/id #uuid "aee759b6-b6d2-5dd6-8b07-1eeb9d8cea24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{4}{3}(y-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11825/selection/047414d6a72d7901faff605d472a0e39fd9957dc6db19cb0c175d95c9649d92f" :answer/id #uuid "41067cb0-fbed-56c3-8885-c0fccaf92259" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{2}{3}(y-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11825/selection/e82ce9afb1515982f57ec23e38157fb91cac378a900670095a7fa70e98f231fc" :answer/id #uuid "1885a63b-a8ef-5e75-9b02-aea3a8bbf160" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}(y-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11825/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f41cdd0-f785-5276-a2dd-e104ff774145" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11825/selection/b84dbb196368112b67963012d5eb95628a68cbc3e7ebc3754fae1a2791231677" :answer-field/choices ["q-11825/selection/3d4912fba6865d84fff42ae1218f5bc1017b36b705fe0ea683a0de996c2d48c0" "q-11825/selection/82ae299ea8c2505291695068a185902058180804be81fb94e5f22ded483c2bcf" "q-11825/selection/b84dbb196368112b67963012d5eb95628a68cbc3e7ebc3754fae1a2791231677" "q-11825/selection/047414d6a72d7901faff605d472a0e39fd9957dc6db19cb0c175d95c9649d92f" "q-11825/selection/e82ce9afb1515982f57ec23e38157fb91cac378a900670095a7fa70e98f231fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11825" :question/id #uuid "fc87e31d-742b-5368-879d-59099aad814b" :question/math-academy-id "q-11825" :question/problem "Find the equation of the downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,4)$ and which passes through the point $(4,-8).$" :question/worked-solution "For any upward or downward-opening parabola with its vertex at $(h,k),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nHere, the vertex has coordinates $(h,k)=(0,4).$ Substituting these into the general standard equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-0)^{2} & =4p(y-4) \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4p(y-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left to find the value of $p.$ We know that the given parabola also passes through the point $(4,-8),$ so we can substitute $x=4$ and $y=-8$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4p(y-4) \\\\ {4}^{2} & =4p(-8-4) \\\\ 16 & =-48p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4p(y-4) \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{3})(y-4) \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-\\frac{4}{3}(y-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11825/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29e2083d-fe76-5a35-9c3a-7e6ad19ff968"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11825"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11835/selection/f9135876c566daf06fbf795e97a039becf178eff1310910ab5e05527462a9765" :answer/id #uuid "374d3009-80c0-5e95-863c-a90e4e06cc50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}=\\frac{16}{3}(y-6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11835/selection/651d70d94e1d6abb6290be333c7a4283cd475391d1b813c603ba663df1ca8a4b" :answer/id #uuid "0b20a6ad-59e3-5654-afe8-d0b0c8adf5e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}=-\\frac{16}{3}(y-6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11835/selection/be2c351cea3a35d50e80de1c66d6bccebead5c802f78c42d12b0730ecceab30a" :answer/id #uuid "793c30b3-5402-591f-8570-ec252642ae9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}=\\frac{8}{3}(y-6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11835/selection/2df1ec96d6668733848bd2f6b3c912a105a4b51e619c96fce65886f3afe4d0d3" :answer/id #uuid "8ebfafec-fe91-59c8-9712-a27db206390a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}=-\\frac{8}{3}(y-6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11835/selection/d90e06e1ba41b8e307fa60bbe7653b747837c6e28af2fefa540eb44b89ea295c" :answer/id #uuid "c2ec1a6c-c904-575d-a89c-8d3adb38cefa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-6)^{2}=-\\frac{16}{3}(y+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11835/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1f9866c1-7043-5e63-8942-adf48f17c18b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11835/selection/651d70d94e1d6abb6290be333c7a4283cd475391d1b813c603ba663df1ca8a4b" :answer-field/choices ["q-11835/selection/f9135876c566daf06fbf795e97a039becf178eff1310910ab5e05527462a9765" "q-11835/selection/651d70d94e1d6abb6290be333c7a4283cd475391d1b813c603ba663df1ca8a4b" "q-11835/selection/be2c351cea3a35d50e80de1c66d6bccebead5c802f78c42d12b0730ecceab30a" "q-11835/selection/2df1ec96d6668733848bd2f6b3c912a105a4b51e619c96fce65886f3afe4d0d3" "q-11835/selection/d90e06e1ba41b8e307fa60bbe7653b747837c6e28af2fefa540eb44b89ea295c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11835" :question/id #uuid "f9d40cb8-4907-57fa-84f1-cf5c810e6713" :question/math-academy-id "q-11835" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974277/assets/2819ceb4214f8df19ef349794c243771a1080bccf0bf2bbdbdbca9be67d4fbdb.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "We know that for any upward or downward-opening parabola with its vertex at $(h,k),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nHere, the vertex has coordinates $(h,k)=(-4,6).$ Substituting these into the general standard equation, we get\n\n$$\n(x+4)^{2}=4p(y-6).\n$$\n\nWe are left to find the value of $p.$ We know that the given parabola also passes through the point $(4,-6),$ so we can substitute $x=4$ and $y=-6$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2} & =4p(y-6) \\\\ (4+4)^{2} & =4p(-6-6) \\\\ 64 & =-48p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2} & =4p(y-6) \\\\ (x+4)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{4}{3})(y-6) \\\\ (x+4)^{2} & =-\\frac{16}{3}(y-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11835/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a991a3b1-6de7-5978-9dd6-cb9eb3f183a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11835"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11837/selection/aae6df4caf555bcadc9b5a099378f3b8cb7b35f5fd59512c3633e938acce776d" :answer/id #uuid "409d28b3-4e6b-5ff4-adb4-aa7f343ec8ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+6)^{2}=9(y+6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11837/selection/b3b64ab65a3ea0eb30f9341ee5bd92962135c861eae9839349270d98d02fab13" :answer/id #uuid "038954da-ce71-5955-b007-6c26a619984e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-6)^{2}=9(y-6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11837/selection/1c4a241168dba