rtex has coordinates $(h,k)=(-6,-6).$ Substituting these into the general standard equation, we get\n\n$$\n(x+6)^{2}=4p(y+6).\n$$\n\nWe are left to find the value of $p.$ We know that the given parabola also passes through the point $(0,-2),$ so we can substitute $x=0$ and $y=-2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+6)^{2} & =4p(y+6) \\\\ (0+6)^{2} & =4p(-2+6) \\\\ 36 & =16p \\\\ p & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+6)^{2} & =4p(y+6) \\\\ (x+6)^{2} & =4(\\frac{9}{4})(y+6) \\\\ (x+6)^{2} & =9(y+6).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11837/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a991a3b1-6de7-5978-9dd6-cb9eb3f183a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11837"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
